Myth: **The First Bridge**

Before the River Keepers, there was only the First Bridge—a span of rope and wood connecting two isolated peoples.

The Westbank elder stood at the bridge's edge, holding four of her five precious grain sacks. Her people were hungry, but the Eastbank had the knowledge to multiply grain through sacred cultivation. The blessing of the bridge was this: any grain carried across would triple by the time it reached the other side.

She tied the four sacks to the rope and sent them sliding across the chasm. Her heart pounded as she watched them disappear into the Eastbank mists. She kept one sack—barely enough for her people to survive if the Eastbank kept everything.

Now came the waiting.

The Eastbank elder received twelve sacks where four had been sent. He stood surrounded by abundance, facing his choice. He could keep it all—his people would feast while the Westbank starved. Or he could honor the risk the Westbank elder had taken.

The First Bridge swayed in the wind, patient and silent.

